(t) = Φu(t)$\n> $L2$: $x_{p}^{′}(t) = Φu^{′}(t) + Φ^{′}u(t)$\n> $L3$: $Φu^{′}(t) + Φ^{′}u(t) = AΦu(t) + f(t)$\n> $L4$: $Φ^{′} = AΦ$\n> $L5$: $Φu^{′}(t) = f(t)$\n> $L6$: $u^{′}(t) = Φ^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n> $L7$: $u(t) = \\displaystyle \\intΦ^{-1}f(t)dt$\n> $L8$: $x_{p}(t) = Φ\\displaystyle \\intΦ^{-1}f(t)dt$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nLine $L2$ follows from line $L1$ by {{field-1}} both sides of the equation.\n\nLine $L3$ is obtained by substituting $L1$ and $L2$ into the {{field-2}}.\n\nLine $L6$ follows from line $L5$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\nLine $L4$ follows from the fact that {{field-4}} matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af8cf798-4327-5f5b-82ab-f622f20ccc38" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous Boundary Value Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "944bf8ed-46b7-55b7-9ae7-f3686f03d94d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149920} {:answer/id #uuid "3b51d554-2a7e-5113-a1a9-745a3657fa28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149921}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2f42c2ad-4295-5c76-9034-69c1ed9b17f2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149919} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b4d8744-68d8-54ae-a159-8c21bede4028" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149923} {:answer/id #uuid "494865e3-dfc1-541f-9ff5-5d9f025d0fac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149924}] :answer-field/id #uuid "96f4839c-09e1-50b0-aed6-3bdd704ddc14" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149922} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da9aa752-15cc-53a4